<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Toffa I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1908</span> · Also known as King Toffa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Toffa I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto-novo">Porto-Novo</a>, on the coast of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a>, from 1874 until his death in 1908. Threatened by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-dahomey">Dahomey</a> and by British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lagos">Lagos</a>, he renewed the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> over his kingdom in 1882 and supported the French in their war against Dahomey in 1890–94. Under French rule Porto-Novo became the capital of the colony of Dahomey, and Toffa's royal powers were gradually reduced.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/toffa-i.jpg" alt="Toffa I" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: photographe non identifié · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roi_Toffa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
